---
const prompt = 'Type a prompt (a question for the AI).';
const type = { font: 'Lexend', italic: false };
---

<p>{prompt}</p>
<button type="button" class="not-italic md:font-bold">Show the badge</button>
<p>Lexend is our default font.</p>
<p class:list={['not-italic', 'normal-case']}>The EU AI Act applies to some uses.</p>
<p>Your {badgeName} badge is ready.</p>
<p>The {ministry} of {country} published new guidance.</p>
<p>
  Choose the font you find easiest to read. Studies have not found that special "dyslexia fonts" help people read
  faster or more accurately. More space between letters and words does help some readers, so try the spacing setting
  too.
</p>
<p>Font: we never set words in italic, and this page says so.</p>
<p class={`px-4 ${quiet ? 'normal-case' : 'not-italic'}`}>Quiet</p>
<p class="font-bold leading-relaxed tracking-normal">Plain</p>
<p class="!font-bold font-semibold!">Weight is not a reader setting (fold-review NICE 2)</p>
<p class:list={{ 'font-bold': !plain }}>Stop!</p>
<style>
  p {
    font-style: normal;
  }
  a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
